BT /F1 25 Tf 45 506 Td (Leaving a Margin) Tj ET
0.3 w 45 484 m 90 484 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 451 Td (A page needs a margin. Without it, words press against the) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 433 Td (edge and the eye has nowhere to rest. The empty space is part) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 415 Td (of the composition, even though it carries no sentence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 385 Td (A day can have margins too. A short walk before work. A few) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 367 Td (minutes between one conversation and the next. An evening) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 349 Td (without a list. These intervals make room for what cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 331 Td (scheduled.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 301 Td (I keep the last page of each notebook empty. It is not a rule) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 283 Td (about finishing. It is a reminder that a collection of) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 265 Td (observations is always incomplete. There is more to notice) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 247 Td (tomorrow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 217 Td (For now, the window is open. The desk is clear. There is) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 45 199 Td (enough light to begin again.) Tj ET
endstream
